stremio for Debian - Source Package Notes
==========================================

+ds tarball: data/server.js excluded
-------------------------------------

Upstream's git tree bundles data/server.js, a 6.6MB webpack-minified
JavaScript blob with no corresponding source in this repository (its
preferred form for modification lives in the separate stremio-server
upstream project). This is excluded from the +ds tarball via
Files-Excluded in debian/copyright.

At runtime the application reads the SERVER_PATH environment variable
(src/server.rs) to find server.js and spawn it with `node`. The
debian/stremio-wrapper script sets SERVER_PATH to
/usr/share/stremio/server.js.

server.js itself is not freely redistributable (see
stremio-server-installer's own debian/README.source for the full
investigation), so this package does not, and cannot, Depend: on a
Debian package that ships it. Instead, this package Recommends:
stremio-server-installer, a contrib package that downloads server.js
from Stremio's own servers onto the user's machine at install time
(modeled on ttf-mscorefonts-installer/virtualbox-ext-pack). Without it,
stremio still runs, but BitTorrent-based streaming is unavailable.

No vendored Rust dependencies
------------------------------

Unlike stremio-gtk (the CEF-based sibling package), this package vendors
nothing: every crate dependency is satisfied by a librust-*-dev package
in Debian's archive. See debian/patches for the two Cargo.toml patches
that pin a handful of direct dependencies to the exact versions Debian
ships instead of upstream's slightly newer pins.
